---
// firma2-provenance — one quiet line under a value the system worked out:
// how it was arrived at and from what, then (after a middle dot) the edition
// or the shapes it covers. "Measured from the work areas", "Estimated with
// Restoration carbon · 2026.1", "Subwatershed · Upland buffer unit".
//
// WHO READS IT, AND WHY IT IS NOT "TEXT ABOUT THE PAGE". The record holds
// three kinds of figure — typed by a person, measured off the shapes,
// estimated by a method — and they look identical as numbers. A reader who
// takes a measured 62 acres for a reported one makes exactly the mistake the
// brief's "Only compare two things the record actually holds" exists to stop,
// so the line passes the cut-by-default test: without it, the reader errs.
// It is about the value, never about the page; it carries no time stamp,
// because a live derivation is always "now" and "· today" would be a constant.
//
// TWO HALVES, ONE COMPONENT. This file renders the line on the server; the
// record's derived values are mostly painted in the browser (they rerun as
// work areas are drawn), so src/lib/provenance.ts builds the identical
// markup there. Both import firma2-provenance.css; change the look in one
// place.
//
// bcn-lego-checked: see firma2-provenance.css — no esa- lego is a source
// line; Beacon is not cloned on this machine.
import './firma2-provenance.css';

interface Props {
  /** How the value was arrived at, and from what. Front-loaded. */
  source: string;
  /** The edition, or which shapes it covers. Optional. */
  detail?: string;
  /** Inline in a one-line cell rather than its own line. */
  inline?: boolean;
}

const { source, detail, inline = false } = Astro.props;
const text = detail ? `${source} · ${detail}` : source;
const Tag = inline ? 'span' : 'p';
---
<Tag class="firma2-provenance typography-body-sm" data-inline={inline ? '' : undefined}>{text}</Tag>
